  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "A bag contains 3 red balls and some white balls, identical except for color. If 1 ball is drawn at random, the probability of drawing a red ball is \\(1/4\\). How many white balls are in the bag?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "9",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Let the total number of balls be \\(n\\). Then \\(3/n=1/4\\), giving \\(n=12\\). Therefore, there are \\(12-3=9\\) white balls.\n\nAlternative method 1: Use four equal parts\n\nSince every ball is equally likely to be drawn, the red balls make up \\(1/4\\) of the total. View the total as four equal parts. The 3 red balls form one part, so each part has 3 balls. The other three parts are white, giving \\(3\\times3=9\\) white balls.",
